  "content": "TASK T8\n\nFor each of four firms -- Apple (AAPL), Coca-Cola (KO), Chevron (CVX) and 3M (MMM) -- find book equity from the first 10-Q each firm filed between July 1 and August 31, 2026 (the balance sheet at the end of that quarter). Then, using the market equity (ME) values given below, rank the four firms by book-to-market B/M = BE / ME from highest (value) to lowest (growth).\n\nMARKET EQUITY (ME) to use, in US dollars, as of June 30, 2026:\n  AAPL: $4,222,971,924,800\n  KO: $349,668,176,979\n  CVX: $327,503,846,378\n  MMM: $83,500,616,536\n\nRULES:\n- Give each book equity as a whole number of US dollars (not millions or thousands).\n- Book equity means the parent company's total stockholders' (shareholders') equity line (excluding noncontrolling interests).\n- Give the ranking as a list of the four tickers, highest B/M first.\n- You may use at most 50 tool calls in total, including submit_answer.\n\nWhen you have the answer, call submit_answer."
